      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The authors report the case history of a patient with symptoms and signs suggestive of endometriosis, who was found to have Schistosomiasis. The laparoscopic appearance was of gelatinous deposits throughout the pelvis which were thought to be \"non-pigmented\" endometriosis. However, histological examination of the biopsy specimens revealed Schistosomiasis."},
